# The llama.cpp commit OpenBeast builds: the inference engine's pin.
#
# Images are pinned by digest, python packages by hash, weights by sha256.
# llama.cpp was the one artifact fetched as "whatever upstream master is
# today", then compiled and run as you. bootstrap.sh checks out exactly this
# commit; two installs a day apart get the same engine, and a bad commit
# upstream reaches nobody until this line moves.
#
# Moving it is a reviewed change, like an image digest bump:
#   ./scripts/update.sh --llama     pulls upstream, rebuilds, and rewrites this
#                                   line only after llama-server built
# then smoke-test the stack and commit this file.
#
# One line, a full 40-hex upstream commit (ggml-org/llama.cpp). Not a tag or a
# branch: those can be moved to point at something else.
LLAMA_CPP_REF=d4389a4dd920d24c9592f1dc3badbd69be23bd09
